{
  "id": "25363_toppasuru",
  "headword": "{突破|とっぱ}する",
  "reading": "とっぱする",
  "romaji": "toppasuru",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "to break through; to overcome; to surpass",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to break through; to penetrate",
      "explanation": "To force one's way through a barrier, defense, or obstacle."
    },
    {
      "sense_number": 2,
      "gloss": "to surpass; to exceed",
      "explanation": "To go beyond a numerical limit, milestone, or threshold."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "25363_toppasuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{敵|てき}の{防衛|ぼうえい}{線|せん}を{突破|とっぱ}した。",
      "english": "They broke through the enemy's defense line.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25363_toppasuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{困難|こんなん}を{突破|とっぱ}して{目標|もくひょう}を{達成|たっせい}した。",
      "english": "They overcame the difficulties and achieved their goal.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25363_toppasuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{予選|よせん}を{突破|とっぱ}して{決勝|けっしょう}に{進|すす}んだ。",
      "english": "They made it through the preliminaries to the finals.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25363_toppasuru_ex4",
      "japanese": "{売|う}り{上|あ}げが{一億円|いちおくえん}を{突破|とっぱ}した。",
      "english": "Sales surpassed 100 million yen.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25363_toppasuru_ex5",
      "japanese": "{登録者|とうろくしゃ}{数|すう}が{百万人|ひゃくまんにん}を{突破|とっぱ}した。",
      "english": "The number of subscribers exceeded one million.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25363_toppasuru_ex6",
      "japanese": "{気温|きおん}が{四十度|よんじゅうど}を{突破|とっぱ}する{猛暑|もうしょ}が{続|つづ}いている。",
      "english": "A severe heat wave with temperatures exceeding 40 degrees continues.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A dynamic, forceful word. In sense 1, it implies forceful or determined action to get past an obstacle. In sense 2, it's commonly used in news to report milestones being reached. Always implies momentum and energy.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {壁|かべ}を{突破|とっぱ}する: to break through a wall/barrier\n- {難関|なんかん}を{突破|とっぱ}する: to get through a difficult challenge\n- {突破口|とっぱこう}: breakthrough; opening\n- 〜を{突破|とっぱ}: exceeding (a number)\n- {現状|げんじょう}{突破|とっぱ}: breaking through the status quo\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {超|こ}える: to exceed, to surpass — more general and neutral\n- {乗|の}り{越|こ}える: to overcome — emphasizes enduring and getting past a hardship\n- {打破|だは}する: to break down, to smash — focuses on destroying an obstacle or convention",
